<b>Hello this is a bold tag</b>
    <i>Hello this is a italic tag</i>
    <sup>heloo  this is a superscript tag</sup>
    <sub>hello  this is a subscript tag</sub>
    <ol>it is a order list it will gives you a list with numbers</ol>
    <ul>this is under list this will gives you list with bullets</ul>
    <li>this is a list item</li>
    <a href="">it is a anchor tag it will connet to you any link thriugh href attribute</a>
    if you will use target="_blank" as a attribute in <a></a> the link will open on another tab
    pseudo elements  are used to add some style to your element like ::before and ::after
    pseudo classes are  used to add some style to your element when it is in a certain state like :hover and :focus
